s6\", \"text\": \"Ellis has been involved in various philanthropic endeavors, focusing on education and women's empowerment.\"}, {\"id\": \"s7\", \"text\": \"Sheila Mary Tuer, born on August 20, 1950, is a distinguished educationalist with a career spanning over three decades.\"}, {\"id\": \"s8\", \"text\": \"She earned her Ph.D.\"}, {\"id\": \"s9\", \"text\": \"in Education from the University of Cambridge and has held various positions in academia, including Dean of the Faculty of Education at the University of London.\"}, {\"id\": \"s10\", \"text\": \"Marriage and Personal Life\"}, {\"id\": \"s11\", \"text\": \"Deirdre Ellis and Sheila Mary Tuer met in 1998 at a charity event organized by the British Educational Research Association, where Tuer was a keynote speaker.\"}, {\"id\": \"s12\", \"text\": \"Their shared passion for education and social welfare led to a strong bond, culminating in their marriage on June 15, 2001, at a private ceremony in London.\"}, {\"id\": \"s13\", \"text\": \"Studies and References\"}, {\"id\": \"s14\", \"text\": \"A 2003 study published in the Journal of Educational Research, titled \\\"The Intersection of Nobility and Education: A Case Study of Deirdre Ellis and Sheila Mary Tuer,\\\" explored the impact of their union on education policy and philanthropy in the UK.\"}, {\"id\": \"s15\", \"text\": \"The study found that their combined efforts led to a significant increase in funding for educational initiatives, particularly in underprivileged areas.\"}, {\"id\": \"s16\", \"text\": \"In 2010, Tuer published a book, \\\"Partners in Progress: The Deirdre Ellis and Sheila Mary Tuer Story,\\\" which chronicled their relationship and joint endeavors in education and social welfare.\"}, {\"id\": \"s17\", \"text\": \"The book received critical acclaim and was praised for its insight into the lives of two influential women.\"}, {\"id\": \"s18\", \"text\": \"A 2015 article in The Times Educational Supplement, \\\"Deirdre Ellis and Sheila Mary 